  "answer_text": "Because the phrase **\"iCloud control\"** can refer to a few different tools or actions depending on your operating system, here is a breakdown of the most common meanings and how to use them:\n\n---\n\n### 1. iCloud for Windows (Formerly \"iCloud Control Panel\")\nIf you are on a Windows PC, Apple's official software to manage your iCloud data was historically called the **iCloud Control Panel**. It is now simply known as **iCloud for Windows**. \n\n* **What it does:** It syncs your Apple data with your PC. \n* **Key Features:**\n  * **iCloud Drive:** Access and organize your files directly within Windows File Explorer.\n  * **iCloud Photos:** View and download your photos, which integrate directly into the Windows Photos app.\n  * **iCloud Passwords:** Autofill and manage passwords in Chrome, Edge, or Firefox using the iCloud Passwords extension.\n  * **Mail, Contacts, and Calendars:** Sync your Apple calendar and contact info to Microsoft Outlook.\n* **How to get it:** You can download it for free from the **Microsoft Store** or directly from Apple's support website.\n\n---\n\n### 2. \"iCloud Control\" Utility (For macOS Selective Sync)\nIf you are on a Mac and searching for **iCloud Control**, you might be looking for the popular, open-source third-party utility. \n\n* **What it does:** macOS natively manages iCloud Drive automatically, sometimes offloading files to the cloud to save space when it feels like it. The **iCloud Control** app gives you manual, selective control over your iCloud Drive files.\n* **Key Features:** It adds a dedicated widget or Finder menu that allows you to force-download files to keep them offline, or instantly evict local copies to free up storage space.\n* **How to get it:** It is hosted on GitHub and can be easily installed via Homebrew on Mac using the terminal command:\n  ```bash\n  brew install --cask icloud-control\n  ```\n\n---\n\n### 3. Controlling Your iCloud Settings (iPhone, iPad, Mac, and Web)\nIf you simply want to manage your iCloud storage, backups, and synced apps, you can access your native \"control center\" for iCloud on any device:\n\n* **On iPhone or iPad:** Go to **Settings** > **[Your Name]** (at the very top) > **iCloud**. From here, you can toggle which apps sync, manage your iCloud+ subscription, or clean up storage.\n* **On Mac:** Click the **Apple Menu (\uf8ff)** > **System Settings** > **[Your Name]** > **iCloud**.\n* **On any browser:** Go to **[iCloud.com](https://www.icloud.com)**. This web-based control panel allows you to check your Mail, Photos, and Drive, and use \"Find My\" to locate lost devices.",
